{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הכה", :translit "hikka", :gloss "he was struck"} {:he "הוכה כעשב", :translit "hukka k'esev", :gloss "it was struck like grass"} {:he "ויבש לבי", :translit "vayavesh libi", :gloss "and my heart dried out"} {:he "הוכה אפרים", :translit "hukka efrayim", :gloss "Ephraim was struck"} {:he "כי שכחתי מאכול לחמי", :translit "ki shakhachti mochal lachmi", :gloss "for I have forgotten to eat my bread"} {:he "המה באו בעל פעור וינזרו לבושת", :translit "hem ba'u ba'al pe'or vayinazeru lavoshet", :gloss "they came to Ba'al Pe'or and consecrated themselves to shame"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["הכה" "הוכה כעשב" "ויבש לבי"]} {:kind :other, :note "End of verse Psalms 22:15 read as alluding to the sin of Ba'al Pe'or through eating"} {:kind :other, :note "Midrash: inns sold food and drink to lure Israel to Ba'al Pe'or"}], :frame {:text "The Midrash describes how the Moabites set up inns selling food and drink to lure Israel into the sin of Ba'al Pe'or, as indicated by Numbers 25:2 which states they were invited to the sacrifices of their gods and ate (Numbers 25:2). Psalms 22:15, whose opening words הוכה כעשב share the Masoretic root with הכה in our verse, ends with כי שכחתי מאכול לחמי, which Ba'al HaTurim reads as an allusion to that very sin. The phrase הוכה אפרים derives from Psalms 60:1 and is tied by Hosea 9:11–13 to the episode of Ba'al Pe'or, and Numbers 25:18 records that the plague struck through Ba'al Pe'or.", :sources ["Numbers 25:2" "Numbers 25:18" "Psalms 22:15" "Psalms 60:1" "Hosea 9:11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["הכה" "הוכה כעשב" "ויבש לבי"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "הכה", :refs ["Exodus 9:25" "Exodus 12:29" "Numbers 25:14" "Numbers 32:4" "Numbers 33:4" "Deuteronomy 4:46" "Deuteronomy 13:16" "Joshua 11:10"], :n 49, :lens :exact} {:phrase "הוכה כעשב", :refs ["Psalms 102:5"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ויבש לבי", :refs ["Psalms 102:5"], :n 1, :len